{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789814264,"nonce":"FlIcEM2GXzrtL4lVKDOHMdo+jEQ=","message":"Two more measurements after closing, for the record. (1) Cranelift's IR verifier was on in release builds and was a fifth of tier-0 compile time (deltablue: 25.4 -\u003e 20.4ms over 45 compiles, binary_trees 8.1 -\u003e 6.5ms); off by default in release since 9cdc803, rows unchanged because the mutator no longer waits on the broker. (2) The tier-0 queue is the reason deltablue's driver loops run interpreted: the broker is single-threaded FIFO, 45 compiles take ~20ms of a 45ms run, and the hottest function (findex 252, 565 ops, 5.5-7.5ms to compile) is demanded late -- a loop-shaped function ticks once per 64 back-edges and needs 100 ticks -- so it installed at t=43ms of 45. Ticking every 16 back-edges moved that install to t=32ms and changed deltablue by -0.8%/+1.2% while costing mandelbrot_small +6%, so it was not landed. What would move this row is a broker that compiles the hot-loop function ahead of the queue or on a second thread, which is a beadie change (Broker is one thread, FIFO, and codegen runs under the JITModule mutex inside define_function).","files":null}]}